=== QT008 QT009 QT013 | juxtaposed with a string, which the masked view cannot see
a1:til "3"
a2:where "ab"
a3:flip "ab"

=== QT012 QT008 | a one-char string is an atom, and a symbol vector is not a count
a4:distinct "a"
a5:til `a`b

=== clean | the string shapes q accepts
b1:sum "ab"
b2:distinct "ab"
b3:where ""
b4:til `a
b5:til 0x01
b6:ratios "ab"

=== clean | a builtin name inside a string followed by a string is not a call
s:("x til ";"3")

=== QT014 | the infix form, which is how rotate is written
r:3.5 rotate 1 2

=== QT017 | a char is no window size, infix too
r:"a" mavg 1 2 3

=== QT019 | within with a three-item right operand
r:x within 1 2 3

=== QT018 | cor of two literal vectors of different lengths
r:1 2 cor 1 2 3

=== QT014 | a name before the literal does not change which operand it is
r:f 1.5 rotate 1 2

=== QT014 | nor does a statement before it on the line
r:2 mavg 1 2 3;r2:3.5 rotate 1 2

=== clean | the infix forms q accepts
r1:1 rotate 1 2
r2:2 mavg 1 2 3
r3:x within 1 2
r4:1 2 cor 1 2
r5:1 rotate 1 2,3

=== clean | an infix right operand that runs on is not the literal
r:x within 1 2 3,4


=== clean | an int vector counts (q 5: where 1 2i is 0 1 1)
r:where 1 2i

=== QT009 | a short one does not (q 5: where 1 2h is 'type)
r:where 1 2h

=== QT009 | nor does an atom (q 5: where 2 is 'type)
r:where 2

=== QT009 | a boolean atom either (q 5: where 1b is 'type)
r:where 1b

=== clean | an enlisted atom is a list (q 5: where enlist 2 is 0 0)
r:where enlist 2
